/-
# Order bound for 2-groups with abelian subgroups of bounded rank (Kourovka Notebook Problem 19.75)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 19.75 (B. Sambale): let `P` be a finite
`2`-group of exponent `2^e` such that the rank of every abelian subgroup is at most `r`. Is it true
that `|P| ≤ 2^{r(e+1)}`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGroupAbelianRankOrderBoundKourovka19Problem75Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 19.75 (B.
Sambale). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701623 (`KOU-19.75`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The rank of an abelian group is its least number of generators, so "rank at most `r`" means
generated by at most `r` elements; the exponent is Mathlib's `Monoid.exponent`.
-/

/-- Kourovka 19.75 (B. Sambale): a finite `2`-group `P` of exponent `2^e` in which every abelian
subgroup has rank at most `r` (is generated by `r` elements) has order at most `2^{r(e+1)}`. -/
def twoGroupOrderBoundByAbelianRank : Prop :=
  ∀ (P : Type) [Group P] [Finite P], IsPGroup 2 P → ∀ e r : ℕ, Monoid.exponent P = 2 ^ e →
    (∀ A : Subgroup P, (∀ x ∈ A, ∀ y ∈ A, x * y = y * x) →
      ∃ s : Finset P, s.card ≤ r ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set P) = A) →
    Nat.card P ≤ 2 ^ (r * (e + 1))

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 19.75 "No, it is not true", as follows from
Olshanskii's examples of finite `p`-groups whose abelian subgroups are small compared to the group
(pointed out by Mann). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group
Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems,
Problem 19.75 (B. Sambale); resolution: A. Yu. Olshanskii, The number of generators and orders of
abelian subgroups of finite p-groups, Math. Notes 23 (1978), no. 3, 183-185; A. Mann, letter of 23
April 2018, abstract: the least f(n) such that every finite p-group whose abelian subgroups are
generated by at most n elements has at most f(n) generators grows quadratically in n; Kourovka
Archive, Problem 19.75: No, it is not true, as follows from the examples constructed by Olshanskii
(Mann), https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01651428.
-/
public theorem_wanted twoGroupOrderBoundByAbelianRank_refuted : ¬ twoGroupOrderBoundByAbelianRank

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGroupAbelianRankOrderBoundKourovka19Problem75Wanted
